/ A call in parallel answers a task, and the next step runs before the called goal ends: Slow sleeps, then reads
/ %order% — its reads fall through to the caller's memory, live — so it reads what the step after the call wrote.
/ What the task writes stays in it: the caller's %order% is its own.
Start
- goal.call(Name="Slow", Parallel=true); variable.set(Name=%task%, Value=%!data%)
- variable.set(Name=%order%, Value="caller")
- assert.equals(Expected="task", Actual=%task!type.name%, Message="a call in parallel answers a task")
- task.wait(Task=%task%); variable.set(Name=%result%, Value=%!data%)
- assert.equals(Expected="caller,task", Actual=%result%, Message="the next step ran before the called goal read %order%")
- assert.equals(Expected="caller", Actual=%order%, Message="what the task wrote stayed in it")

Slow
- timer.sleep(Duration="1s")
- variable.set(Name=%order%, Value="%order%,task")
- goal.return(Data=%order%)
